    <statement><p>A manufacturer sells aardvark masks at a price of
$270 per mask and butterfly masks at a price
of $520 per mask.  A quantity of <em>a</em> 
aardvark masks and <em>b</em> butterfly masks is sold
at a total cost of $600 to the manufacturer.</p>
<p>(a) Express the manufacturer's profit, <em>P</em>,
as a function of <em>a</em> and <em>b</em>.</p>
<p><m>P(a,b) =</m> <fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/> dollars.</p>
<p>(b) The curves of constant profit in the ab-plane are
<var form="buttons">
<li>
<p>hyperbolas</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>ellipses</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>circles</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>lines</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>parabolas</p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>270a+520b-600</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
